# M5 edge-degradation condition (scripts/netem.sh). Approved 2026-10-10.
# Applied only to B->A control-plane traffic (:6443, :30090); Locust load (:30080) is untouched.
# - Delay 150 ms on top of the hotspot (baseline RTT median ~20–85 ms, p99 ~180–210 ms): a congested
#   wireless edge uplink.
# - No added jitter: netem jitter reorders packets and triggers TCP spurious retransmissions; the hotspot
#   already supplies natural jitter.
# - Loss 1 %: a lost SYN costs a 1 s retransmit, which meets Prometheus's 1.0 s connect timeout; 2 % would
#   push stale ticks so high that episodes get excluded instead of measured.
# Validity rule (pre-registered): if a dry run under this condition shows > 10 % stale ticks, use 0.5 % loss.
NETEM_DELAY=150ms
NETEM_JITTER=0ms
NETEM_LOSS=1%
